  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Colombia Venezuela Migration Crisis</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A large-scale humanitarian crisis is developing after hundreds of thousands (Venezuelans and Colombians, who had fled Colombia&apos;s armed conflict) have come to Colombia since 2014. They are leaving Venezuela as it is increasingly difficult to access food and medicines. In the last year there has been a marked increase and even more so in the last 4 months where there has been an increase of 50% of people leaving Venezuela. The poorest of the poor have started to leave to avoid starvation. Venezuela does not produce enough food to provide food to their people, and prices on the black market are unaffordable.
SNPS/Caritas Colombia proposed a reduced 6 month project in 5 departments (close to the border and Cundinamarca) - (initially it was 7 departments with 14 municipalities, but it had to be reduced due to a shortcoming in the funds received after the EA). The project has 5 components: 1. Food, 2. non- food items and Shelter, 3. Health, 4. Protection and 5. Advocacy.  Other Caritas agencies contributing to this project which was launched through an EA appeal are Caritas Germany, Caritas Spain, Secours Catholique (Caritas France), Caritas Japan, Caritas Hong Kong and Caritas Korea.</narrative>
  </description>
